{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>וְזָכַרְתִּי לָהֶם בְּרִית וגו׳</b> — our Sages of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim), and this is their language: From where do we know that a covenant was sealed for the tribes? For it is written ״וְזָכַרְתִּי וגו׳ בְּרִית וגו׳ אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵאתִי״ וגו׳. And it is possible to say that the intention is along the lines of the verse's saying (Jeremiah 2:2) ״זָכַרְתִּי לָךְ חֶסֶד נְעוּרַיִךְ אַהֲבַת״ וגו׳, and likewise He said here ״וְזָכַרְתִּי״ וגו׳ — meaning that HaShem will remember for the last generation the merit of the first generation that entered into a covenant with HaShem with great love. And He explained who those first ones, the masters of the covenant, are, and said: them — whom I brought them out וגו׳, and [through whose merit] He is sanctified through their intercession, the living Elohim." "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of BeChukotai</b>, <b>the book of Leviticus is completed</b>."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:47.146742187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}